Assassin's Creed Odyssey is the latest  game in the long-running franchise and  has been confirmed for release in  October this year for Xbox one ps4 and  PC coming hot off the heels of 2017 s  Assassin's Creed origins Odyssey seems  to be changing things up for the series  even more we already had a chance to  play the new game for a few hours and  experience many of its features  so here's six things new and assassin's  creed Odyssey that we think changed the  formula in interesting ways  the Sasa's Creed series is well known  for its historical backdrops this time  we're going acient Greece specifically  we'll be exploring in the year 413 BC in  the midst of the Peloponnesian War its  Sparta versus Athens but you're a  mercenary seeking revenge on those who  took your family away from you you'll be  traveling to lush locations around  Greece like Mykonos Delos and Attica to  name a few and meeting prominent  historical figures like Socrates  Hippocrates and he rode Otis you'll be  able to go through this Odyssey as  either a male protagonist named Alexios  or a female protagonist named Cassandra  they have the same story dialogue and  abilities the only difference is the  voice acting and character models it's a  similar approach to how Mass Effect had  both male and female shepherds  but it's up to you who you'll lead  across ancient Greece  picking the lead character isn't the  only decision you'll be making an  assassin's creed Odyssey for the first  time in franchise history dialog options  will permeate the entire adventure there  will be opportunities to tease out more  information during conversations but  some decisions can impact how the game  plays out certain NPCs can also be  romance or befriended depending on what  you say  Ubisoft toyed with the idea of letting  players know whether or not certain  lines have an effect on outcomes similar  to telltale games but ultimately decided  it would be better for players to not  worry about making the optimal choice  [Music]  there will be consequences to your  actions for example the demo we play  prompted us to align with one or two  characters on how to approach leading a  rebellion  we chose the more subtle approach which  gave us a mission to sneakily take out  enemy weapons and supplies on foot had  we chose decide with the one suggesting  more brute force we would have had to  complete naval combat missions instead  it's not just about what you say to  other characters either side quests are  where it gets interesting  in one case socrates gave us a heads up  on a rebel being held hostage who could  help the fight but he's known to be a  loose cannon we can either free the  rebel kill him or ignore the quest  altogether since we decided to free this  character in the Socrates side quest he  appeared in the conclusion of a main  quest line but straight-up assassinated  an important character during what was  supposed to be a celebration this result  also damaged the relationship we had  with another character we can't say  socrates didn't warn us though that's  just one example of consequences in this  huge open world game  since Greece is a collection of islands  with lots of water to explore in the  middle it makes sense that's sailing  your own ship is core to a sea Odyssey  naval combat will also play a huge role  much like Assassin's Creed 4 Black Flag  expect to destroy enemy ships with fire  aerobridges  waves of javelins or full-speed naval  rams  once ships reach zero health you can  loot them by hopping aboard and engaging  in traditional hand-to-hand combat ac  origins had a few instances of seafaring  battles but Odyssey is treading deeper  waters  [Music]  combat abilities and skill trees give  players plenty of options when it comes  to fights and assassinations holding the  left shoulder button turns the face  buttons into ability activations and the  left trigger does is for bow and arrow  abilities in total eight skills are  available to you at once a few notable  skills are a shield grip a healing  ability and a multi arrow shot but  nothing comes close to the iconic  spartan kick giving enemies the boot  will comically send them flying backward  ideal for launching them off ships or  off the side of a cliff this is sparta  after all these are a few of the new  things we saw with our short time in  ancient Greece so stick the game spot  for more on assassin's creed Odyssey  [Music]
 

